    a: 'It depends on the size of the job and how much prep the site needs. Every quote from Concrete Toronto is free and in writing, so you know the exact price before any work starts.',
  },
  {
    q: 'My postwar bungalow still has its original driveway. What should I expect?',
    a: 'Original postwar concrete has usually earned its retirement. Expect removal, excavation to a proper depth, a compacted base, and a fresh pour. Most North York driveway replacements take a few days on site plus curing time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you pour concrete for an infill or new build?',
    a: 'Yes. We work with homeowners and builders on infill projects across North York: driveways, walkways, porches, slabs and foundation flatwork, scheduled to fit the build.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you handle side-yard walkways on narrow lots?',
    a: 'Yes. North York side yards are often tight, and a properly graded side walkway keeps water away from the foundation. We pour them regularly, straight or curved to fit the space.',
  },
